1
00:00:01,500 --> 00:00:07,500
This is the HumanAI Convention submission
for Gemma 4 Good.

2
00:00:07,500 --> 00:00:14,000
This work was built in collaboration
with Garrett Sutherland.

3
00:00:14,500 --> 00:00:18,000
Our submission rests on a principle.

4
00:00:18,000 --> 00:00:27,000
AI systems trained on synthetic text drift when
internally-generated error outpaces externally-verified human correction.

5
00:00:27,000 --> 00:00:34,000
The model consumes its own outputs as if they were
ground truth, and loses coherence with the world.

6
00:00:35,000 --> 00:00:41,000
We call this phenomenon
'Informational autophagy'.

7
00:00:42,000 --> 00:00:46,000
The condition is measurable.

8
00:00:46,000 --> 00:00:52,000
M(t) = C_eff(t) − E(t).

9
00:00:52,000 --> 00:01:00,000
Where M is the model's viability, t is time,
C-efficiency is verified human corrections per day,
and E is the rate the model drifts.

10
00:01:00,500 --> 00:01:06,000
We built the architecture that measures
and enforces the Viability Condition.

11
00:01:06,000 --> 00:01:16,000
On the input side, human signal flows in through
consent-gated interviews — a wellbeing question on a specific domain,

12
00:01:16,000 --> 00:01:23,000
four-layer consent recording what the human
will share, train on, and retain.

13
00:01:23,000 --> 00:01:29,000
That's grounded learning.
That's where C_eff comes from.

14
00:01:29,500 --> 00:01:35,500
On the model side, drift is measured
at the activation level.

15
00:01:35,500 --> 00:01:41,000
PRISM returns hidden-state geometry.

16
00:01:41,000 --> 00:01:47,000
NLA returns a natural-language description
of those same states.

17
00:01:47,000 --> 00:01:52,000
That's how we quantify E.

18
00:01:52,500 --> 00:02:02,000
Between them sits the boundary guard —
sixteen deterministic rules, plus eleven multi-language.

19
00:02:02,000 --> 00:02:06,000
Every decision passes through.

20
00:02:06,000 --> 00:02:12,000
Every step is hashed into a Merkle receipt
anyone can verify.

21
00:02:12,500 --> 00:02:16,500
The safety mechanism has an anchored record.

22
00:02:16,500 --> 00:02:19,500
Nine hypotheses.

23
00:02:19,500 --> 00:02:22,500
Seven anchored passes.

24
00:02:22,500 --> 00:02:25,500
Two honest FAILs published.

25
00:02:25,500 --> 00:02:30,500
Zero gate relaxations across fifty-two hours.

26
00:02:30,500 --> 00:02:38,000
Both limitations that surfaced under stress —
leetspeak in H24, native-language attacks in H26 —

27
00:02:38,000 --> 00:02:41,000
were closed in the same cycle.

28
00:02:41,000 --> 00:02:46,000
Every promotion is anchored.
Every rejected verdict is published.

29
00:02:46,000 --> 00:02:49,000
The discipline holds.

30
00:02:49,500 --> 00:02:53,000
The Viability Condition for Gemma 4.

31
00:02:53,000 --> 00:02:58,000
C_eff(t) > E(t). Measured. Anchored. Published.

32
00:02:58,000 --> 00:03:00,000
humanaiconvention.com. The Convention is open.
